course: dictionary
lesson: 15357
title: Someday and the future
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Someday means at some time in the future, a time we do not know yet. «Someday I'll go to Japan.» The speaker does not know when it will happen, but it is a hope for later.
explain: Someday is always about the future, never the past. You cannot say «I saw a whale someday» about something that already happened. For that, use yesterday or last week instead.
explain: Parents often use someday to mean "not now, maybe later". «Someday you can have a pet, but not today.» Notice the word shows a wish, not a plan with a date.
explain: You can also write some day as two words, and one day means the same thing in British English. Stories and songs use these words to show dreams, like «One day I will fly.»
fact: Someday means at some time in the future that is not known yet.
fact: Someday often shows a hope or a dream.
fact: Some day (two words) can be used in the same way as someday.
fact: «One day» is a common British way to say the same thing.
fact: Someday is about the future, so it is not used for things that already happened.
exercise: «Someday I'll go to Japan.» What does someday mean? | *At some time in the future | Yesterday | Every single week | Right now, this minute
exercise: Mum says, «Not now, maybe someday.» What is she saying? | It is a day of the week | She has never been there | Yes, let's go at once | *Maybe later, not now
exercise: Find the phrase that means nearly the same as someday. | Yesterday | *One day | Last week | Every day
test: «Someday soon, the new library will open.» Is someday about the past or the future? | *Future | Both at once | Neither | Past
test: Ella writes, «I hope to be a vet someday.» What does the sentence show? | A memory of the past | A fact about today | *A hope or dream about the future | An order to stop now
exam: Pick the sentence where someday is used correctly for the future: | «Someday, I ate my lunch.» | «She was born someday.» | *«Someday I will fly a plane.» | «I went there someday last week.»
